    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. but honestly, some of the officials i'm meeting with are really pretty intense about the \"climate crisis\" angle. they act like if we don't do this right now, everything's doomed. i need to know how to address that. is there any actual evidence that these specific local regulations are even going to make a dent in global emissions, considering we're just one small part of the economy? i want to point out how much of a symbolic gesture this is compared to the actual cost we're facing.",
